# Portal member session contract

Guest **registration** (P6-1) and member **self-service** (P6-3) share the same public-auth session on the **portal host** (`{club}.portal.{root}`).

**Profile architecture (frozen):** [platform-portal-member-profile.mdoc](./platform-portal-member-profile.mdoc) — canonical BFF, SDK capabilities, migration from current split paths.

## Host

| Env | Portal member base |
| --- | ------------------ |
| Dev (canonical) | `http://{club}.portal.localhost:3003` |
| Prod (platform) | `https://{club}.portal.{root}` |
| Prod (custom) | `https://portal.{apex}` via `tenant_domains` · `surface=portal` |

Authority: [p6-host-addressing-architecture.mdoc](p6-host-addressing-architecture.mdoc)

---

## Session (frozen)

| Item | Value |
| ---- | ----- |
| Cookie | `atour_mb_session` (`SESSION_COOKIE_NAMES.member` in `@app-tour/session-client`) · httpOnly · set by portal BFF after `verify-otp` or `register-complete` |
| Operator cookie (web only) | `atour_op_session` — **not** used on portal member routes |
| Actor | JWT `role` claim · typical guest flow creates `member` · `ACTIVE` membership on tenant |
| TTL | Same as operator session policy in `apps/api` identity layer |
| Scope | Tenant-bound — `sessionTenantMatchesHost` on `/me/*` and `/api/me/*` |

### BFF headers to API

Portal BFF routes under `/api/public-auth/*` and `/api/me/*` forward:

```text
x-tenant-id     ← resolved from Host / public tenant context
Authorization   ← session token from cookie (member routes)
```

Portal `/me` is **not** the operator admin panel (`apps/web`). Product rule: operators use `{club}.admin.{root}`; members use portal host. Middleware accepts any valid JWT role on portal host today; **do not** rely on role rejection until explicitly gated (see freeze doc).

---

## Routes (P6-3)

| Route | Auth | Purpose |
| ----- | ---- | ------- |
| `/me/registrations` | member session | List own tour registrations |
| `/me/registrations/[id]` | member session | Detail + receipt upload |
| `/me/profile` | member session | Edit profile fields (capability-driven · see freeze doc) |
| `GET /api/me/registrations` | member session | BFF list proxy |
| `POST /api/me/registrations/[id]/receipt` | member session | Upload offline receipt proof |
| `GET/PATCH /api/me/profile` | member session | **Landed M2** — sole profile BFF |
| `POST /api/public-auth/logout` | none (idempotent) | Clear `atour_mb_session` · **Landed** 2026-07-02 |

API upstream (frozen — reuse Phase 9.5 member filter):

| BFF route | Upstream API | Scope |
| --------- | ------------ | ----- |
| `GET /api/me/registrations` | `GET /bookings?view=mine` | session user + tenant RLS |
| `POST /api/me/registrations/[id]/receipt` | `POST /bookings/{registrationId}/receipts` | member-only; ensures pending manual payment then `POST /finance/receipts` |

**BFF steps (frozen):**

1. Read multipart `file` from member.
2. Build `fileKey`: `receipts/{registrationId}/{sanitizedFileName}` (dev/smoke — no MinIO in memory E2E).
3. `POST /bookings/{registrationId}/receipts` with JSON `{ fileKey }` and member session headers (`Authorization`, `x-workspace-id` from JWT `workspace_id`).
4. API verifies booking `submittedByUserId === auth.userId`, ensures pending manual payment (creates default offline debt if none), submits receipt.

**Do not** POST multipart to `/finance/receipts` — finance API expects JSON `{ paymentId, fileKey }` only.

---

## Logout

| Route | Status | Behavior |
| ----- | ------ | -------- |
| `POST /api/public-auth/logout` | **Landed** (2026-07-02) | Clears `atour_mb_session` via `clearSessionCookieOnResponse` · returns `{ ok: true }` · **no** API revoke (parity with operator `POST /api/auth/logout`) |

**Client (member nav):** `MemberLogoutButton` in `/me` layout — `POST /api/public-auth/logout` then `router.push("/")` + `router.refresh()`. Hooks: `data-public-auth-logout` · `data-public-auth-logout-ready="true"` after hydration.

**E2E:** **SMK-PTL-06** — register → `/me/registrations` → `data-public-auth-logout` (hydration-ready) → `POST /api/public-auth/logout` 200 → cookie cleared → middleware `307` on `GET /me/registrations` (no member shell) → `401` on `GET /api/me/registrations`. Smoke servers set `MARKETING_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` to portal `/health` so post-logout `/` redirect does not require marketing `:3002`.

**Middleware:** `/api/public-auth/logout` is **not** behind `/api/me/*` guard — callable without valid session (idempotent clear).

Unauthenticated access to `/me/*` → redirect to `/` (portal home → marketing when no session).

---

## Register success → /me (P6-3-N-008)

After `[data-public-registration-success]` on `/catalog/{tourId}/register`, primary CTA links to `/me/registrations`.

---

## Portal home redirect (P6-3-N-009)

| Condition | `/` behavior |
| --------- | ------------ |
| Valid member session | Redirect `/me/registrations` |
| No session | Show club home or link to marketing `/tours` |

---

## Verification

| ID | Assert |
| -- | ------ |
| MEM-01 | Session cookie set after OTP verify (existing user) |
| MEM-02 | Session cookie set after register-complete (new user) |
| MEM-03 | `GET /me/registrations` 401 without session |
| MEM-04 | Member cannot read another user's registration — `GET /bookings?view=mine` scoped to `submittedByUserId` |
| MEM-05 | Logout clears cookie |

Specs: `apps/portal/test/portal-member-*.spec.ts` · `apps/api/test/portal-member-registrations.spec.ts` · **MEM-04** `apps/api/test/bookings-member-isolation.spec.ts` (`view=mine` never leaks another member's booking row)

